{title: Holy, Holy, Holy! Lord God Almighty}
{artist: Reginald Heber (1783-1826)}
{key: D}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [A]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
[G]Early in the [D]morning our [A]song shall rise to Thee;
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [A]Merciful and [D]mighty!
[Bm]God in three [F#m]Persons, [G]blessed [A]Trini[D]ty!
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [A]All the saints a[D]dore Thee,
[G]Casting down their [D]golden crowns a[A]round the glassy sea;
[D]Cherubim and [Bm]seraphim [A]falling down be[D]fore Thee,
[Bm]Who wert, and [F#m]art, and [G]ever[A]more shalt [D]be.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [A]Though the darkness [D]hide Thee,
[G]Though the eye of [D]sinful man Thy [A]glory may not see,
[D]Only Thou art [Bm]holy; [A]there is none be[D]side Thee,
[Bm]Perfect in [F#m]power, in [G]love, and [A]puri[D]ty.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [A]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
[G]All Thy works shall [D]praise Thy Name, in [A]earth and sky and sea;
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [A]Merciful and [D]mighty!
[Bm]God in three [F#m]Persons, [G]blessed [A]Trini[D]ty!
{eov}
